    "narrative": "Today\u2019s optimization for the Austin Waves highlights **Gunnar Henderson** as our premier start, boasting an elite 81.88 score. His matchup against Avila is arguably the most favorable on the board, bolstered by a high-upside 4.91 xERA opposing starter and a significant 16% park factor bump. While he faces an elite hold pitcher that theoretically dampens his SB ceiling, his leadoff placement and dynamic platoon advantage make him the anchor of our lineup. Following closely, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (79.36) and **Kyle Tucker** (75.35) offer high-floor production, with **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** benefiting significantly from the platoon edge against the southpaw Sears, while **Kyle Tucker** and **Andy Pages** both capitalize on the favorable matchup against Rodriguez. **Josh Lowe** also stands out, with his 68.22 score elevated by a robust 14% platoon adjustment and high-speed indicators that could prove crucial in our pursuit of stolen bases.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Dominic Smith**, who finished with a 50.40 score. Despite a decent platoon matchup against Leahy, he narrowly missed the cut because the current depth of our active roster\u2014specifically the efficient projections for **Drake Baldwin** and **Miguel Vargas**\u2014offered superior category coverage across the board. While **Jorge Polanco** and **Jacob Wilson** posted competitive scores in the mid-40s, they were sidelined primarily due to lower projected efficiency compared to our starters and, in **Jorge Polanco**\u2019s case, a lingering 36% rain risk that further depressed his outlook. We remain particularly cognizant of the slow delivery of opposing pitchers in games featuring **Heliot Ramos**, **Andy Pages**, and **Josh Lowe**, as these situational factors provide the marginal upside necessary to gain ground in the scarce SB category.",
